{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate mental health awareness training for at least one staff member",
        "additional_details": "Making this a legal requirement could help reduce work related stress, improve early intervention, support managers, and protect employees \u2014 especially men, who are statistically less likely to seek help. This law could ensure every workplace has someone equipped to respond appropriately, helping to create safer, healthier working environments across the UK.",
        "background": "We want the Government to make it a legal requirement for at least one staff member to be trained in an accredited mental health awareness course. Workplaces already provide physical safety training, but not a mandatory course for mental health.",
